# The editor's htmx data, generated by `cargo xtask web-data` (do not edit) from the editor
# data htmx ships (0BSD): htmx.org 2.0.11, 4.0.0.
# a|e  majors  name  description
a	4	hx-action	Specifies the URL that receives the request. Use with hx-method or as the shared action for verb-specific attributes.
a	2,4	hx-boost	Converts eligible links and forms to htmx-powered requests while preserving progressive enhancement. Can carry boost-specific request config.
a	4	hx-browser-indicator	Enables the browser native loading indicator for this element's requests when set to true. Requires the browser-indicator extension.
a	4	hx-config	Configures per-request behavior using HCON or JSON. Values are merged into the request config; mode is always reset to the global htmx.config.mode.
a	2,4	hx-confirm	Shows a confirmation dialog before issuing a request. A js: value can run custom confirmation logic.
a	2,4	hx-delete	Issues a DELETE request to the specified URL and swaps the response into the DOM.
a	2,4	hx-disable	Disables selected elements while the request is in flight.
a	2	hx-disabled-elt	The hx-disabled-elt attribute allows you to specify elements that will have the disabled attribute added to them for the duration of the request. The value of this attribute can be:
a	2	hx-disinherit	The default behavior for htmx is to "inherit" many attributes automatically: that is, an attribute such as hx-target may be placed on a parent element, and all child elements will inherit that target.
a	2,4	hx-encoding	Sets the request encoding type. Use multipart/form-data for file uploads.
a	2	hx-ext	The hx-ext attribute enables an htmx extension for an element and all its children.
a	2,4	hx-get	Issues a GET request to the specified URL and swaps the response into the DOM.
a	4	hx-head	Controls how the hx-head extension merges or appends response <head> content.
a	2,4	hx-headers	Adds custom headers to the request. Accepts HCON/JSON, and can evaluate JavaScript expressions with the js: prefix.
a	2,4	hx-history	Opts an element or page out of the history-cache extension when set to false.
a	2,4	hx-history-elt	Marks the element that htmx swaps when restoring browser history. If absent, htmx falls back to the body element.
a	4	hx-ignore	Disables htmx processing for the element and its descendants.
a	2,4	hx-include	Includes additional element values in the request. Accepts CSS selectors, this, and htmx extended selectors.
a	2,4	hx-indicator	Specifies the element or elements that receive the htmx-request class while the request is in flight.
a	2	hx-inherit	The default behavior for htmx is to "inherit" many attributes automatically: that is, an attribute such as hx-target may be placed on a parent element, and all child elements will inherit that target. Some people do not like this feature and instead prefer to explicitly specify…
a	4	hx-live	Runs a reactive expression whenever hx-live observes relevant DOM or state changes. Requires the hx-live extension.
a	4	hx-live:*	Binds a reactive expression to an attribute, property, class, style, text, or HTML update. Requires the hx-live extension.
a	4	hx-method	Specifies the HTTP method to use with hx-action. Valid methods are GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, and QUERY. A verb-specific attribute such as hx-post wins over hx-method.
a	4	hx-morph-skip	Leaves an element untouched during a morph swap. htmx copies no attributes and morphs no children.
a	4	hx-morph-skip-children	Morphs an element's attributes during a morph swap but leaves its children alone.
a	4	hx-nonce	Marks htmx elements as server-rendered trusted markup for the CSP extension nonce gate.
a	2,4	hx-on	Wires inline JavaScript to run when an event fires. Use hx-on:event for any DOM event, or hx-on::event as shorthand for hx-on:htmx:event.
a	2	hx-params	The hx-params attribute allows you to filter the parameters that will be submitted with an AJAX request.
a	2,4	hx-partial	Routes response content to a specific target. Use hx-target or id to choose the destination and hx-swap to choose the swap style.
a	2,4	hx-patch	Issues a PATCH request to the specified URL and swaps the response into the DOM.
a	4	hx-pending	Shows pending content from a template while a request is in flight. Requires the hx-pending extension.
a	2,4	hx-post	Issues a POST request to the specified URL and swaps the response into the DOM.
a	4	hx-preload	Preloads content before the user triggers a request. Requires the preload extension.
a	2,4	hx-preserve	Preserves an element with a stable id across swaps when the response contains a matching element.
a	2,4	hx-prompt	Prompts before a request, sends the answer as the HX-Prompt header, and aborts when the user cancels. Requires the prompt extension.
a	4	hx-ptag	Sets the initial per-element polling tag sent as the HX-PTag request header. Requires the ptag extension.
a	2,4	hx-push-url	Pushes a URL into browser history after a request. Accepts true, false, or a URL.
a	2,4	hx-put	Issues a PUT request to the specified URL and swaps the response into the DOM.
a	4	hx-query	Issues a QUERY request to the specified URL and swaps the response into the DOM.
a	2,4	hx-replace-url	Replaces the current browser history URL after a request. Accepts true, false, or a URL.
a	2	hx-request	The hx-request attribute allows you to configure various aspects of the request via the following attributes: timeout - the timeout for the request, in milliseconds credentials - if the request will send credentials noHeaders - strips all headers from the request
a	2,4	hx-select	Selects the part of the response to swap into the target. The value is a CSS selector.
a	2,4	hx-select-oob	Selects response elements to swap into the page out of band.
a	4	hx-sse:close	Closes an SSE connection when a named event matching the attribute value is received from the server.
a	4	hx-sse:connect	Establishes a persistent Server-Sent Events connection. Defaults to loading immediately, reconnecting with exponential backoff, and pausing on background tabs.
a	4	hx-status	Overrides swap behavior for specific HTTP response status codes. Supports exact codes such as 404 and wildcard patterns such as 50x and 5xx.
a	2,4	hx-swap	Controls how response content is inserted. Supports swap styles such as innerHTML, outerHTML, textContent, beforebegin, afterbegin, beforeend, afterend, innerMorph, outerMorph, outerSync, delete, none, and extension-provided styles.
a	2,4	hx-swap-oob	Marks response elements to swap into the page out of band, outside the normal target.
a	2,4	hx-sync	Synchronizes requests between elements using strategies such as drop, abort, replace, queue first, queue last, and queue all.
a	2,4	hx-target	Specifies where to insert the response content. Accepts CSS selectors, this, and htmx extended selectors such as closest, find, next, and previous.
a	4	hx-targets	Swaps the same response content into all elements matching the selector. Requires the targets extension.
a	2,4	hx-trigger	Controls which event specifications trigger an element's request. Supports filters and modifiers such as delay, throttle, once, changed, from, and target.
a	2,4	hx-validate	Runs HTML5 constraint validation before sending the request.
a	2,4	hx-vals	Adds values to request parameters. Accepts HCON/JSON, and can evaluate JavaScript expressions with the js: prefix.
a	2	hx-vars	NOTE: hx-vars has been deprecated in favor of hx-vals, which is safer by default.
a	4	hx-ws:connect	Establishes a WebSocket connection owned by this element. Requires the WebSocket extension.
a	4	hx-ws:send	Sends form data and hx-vals through the nearest hx-ws:connect, including one on the same element. Any value is ignored. Requires the WebSocket extension.
